--- This module defines status of TEE applications.

--- @kind constants
--- @feature ta-session
fmod APP-STATUS is
  sort AppStatus .

  --- outOfMemory: the memory of the TA is exhausted.  Only the rules of the API functions that
  --- allocate memory (allocateTransientObject, allocOperation, openPersistentObject,
  --- createPersistent, allocatePersistentObjectEnumerator) look at it: they return errorOutOfMemory
  --- instead of allocating.  Every other rule runs as in normal status (except the shared-memory
  --- builtins, which are not in the paper or its artifact), so the program goes on
  --- and its call returns ([Internal Core] 4.3.5), as in the paper artifact.  The rules printed in
  --- the paper require status normal also for the API call and TA invocation rules; with them a TA
  --- stops after a memory error, which contradicts the paper's own results (Tables 10 and 13).
  --- A panic is not stopped by a status condition either: a panic rule leaves the call without a
  --- return value (it consumes the reply of the object, or sets api-call to noCall).
  op normal : -> AppStatus [ctor] .
  op outOfMemory : -> AppStatus [ctor] .
  op panic : -> AppStatus [ctor] .
endfm

view AppStatus from TRIV to APP-STATUS is
  sort Elt to AppStatus .
endv

--- This module defines a kernel class, modeling the TA kernel.

--- @kind state
--- @feature ta-session
omod TA-KERNEL is
  pr OBJECT-ID .
  pr APP-STATUS .
  pr NAT .
  pr TEE-API-CALL .

  --- The call status (api-call) has the states noCall, init, exec, final and return.
  class TAKernel | status : AppStatus, storage : Oid,
                   os-kernel : Oid, counter : Nat,
                   api-call : CallStatus .
endom

--- This module defines the TA kernel behavior.

--- @kind behavior
--- @feature ta-session
omod TA-KERNEL-BEHAVIOR is
  pr TA-KERNEL .

  var TK : Oid .

--- TrustedApp can be in out-of-memory at any time.

  --- rl [out-of-memory] :
  ---   < TK : TAKernel | status : normal >
  ---   =>
  ---   < TK : TAKernel | status : outOfMemory >
  --- .

endom
